    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60136" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρόσσαι</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῶν</span>, αἱ, prob. =
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>stepped copings of
			parapets</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κρόσσας μὲν πύργων ἔρυον καὶ ἔρειπον
					ἐπάλξεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					12.258
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κροσσάων ἐπέβαινον</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				444
			</span></i> (expld. by <i><span class="en">
				Aristarch.
			</span></i> as <i>scaling ladders</i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>courses, steps</i> of the Pyramids, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.125
			</span></i>.</div>
